WEBVTT

00:14.660 --> 00:18.450
Well, now. A secret drawer.

00:19.360 --> 00:22.910
It looks like my hunch was right.

00:23.710 --> 00:27.130
Is this a call from someone?

00:27.860 --> 00:31.420
The assassin who shot at me, perhaps?

00:34.250 --> 00:36.010
Your hunch?

00:36.520 --> 00:41.970
You have no proof, do you? 
You just hope I'll give myself away.

00:44.740 --> 00:45.990
So what if I do?

00:45.990 --> 00:49.110
Your bravado won't fool me,

00:49.980 --> 00:54.320
but I'll make use of whatever I can, too.

00:54.730 --> 00:55.780
Answer it.

00:56.500 --> 00:58.660
This had better not be a bomb.

00:58.660 --> 01:01.290
Use the red button to make a call.

01:01.290 --> 01:03.370
Oh, to hell with it!

01:04.890 --> 01:06.960
<i>Have I caught you at a bad time?</i>

01:08.000 --> 01:09.370
I know this voice.

01:09.370 --> 01:14.760
No, it's fine. Share the 
information with him, as well.

01:15.640 --> 01:20.550
Well, now. You seem to have a 
deep affinity for our shop.

01:21.450 --> 01:25.390
We appreciate your patronage, Solitaire-sama.

01:25.890 --> 01:27.320
Grocer!

01:27.770 --> 01:28.840
So,

01:28.840 --> 01:30.690
I assume there's been activity?

01:31.270 --> 01:34.400
All the items you reserved are now in stock.

01:34.750 --> 01:37.740
A record of Metropolitan 
Police communications.

01:37.740 --> 01:42.040
It contains two items 
you'll wish to know about.

01:42.880 --> 01:45.450
The first is ongoing.

01:45.780 --> 01:51.460
Inspector Tsubaki Iwanome seems to be 
speaking with ex-IA Inspector Hosorogi.

01:53.080 --> 01:56.380
<i>Hosorogi! What a name to come up here!</i>

01:56.950 --> 02:00.050
I see. Hosorogi's alive, then.

02:00.050 --> 02:03.370
I will transmit a record of 
the call to you presently.

02:03.690 --> 02:05.080
As for the other item,

02:05.410 --> 02:10.020
Senior Commissioner Habaki received many 
calls from the Shibuya intermediary.

02:10.350 --> 02:14.170
I expected that. I appreciate your work.

02:14.560 --> 02:15.600
We appreciate your business.

02:18.420 --> 02:21.370
A direct line to the Grocer?

02:21.910 --> 02:24.060
Would you consider selling it to me?

02:24.060 --> 02:24.700
No.

02:26.560 --> 02:29.930
I heard you were broad-minded, 
Superintendent General...

02:30.430 --> 02:34.400
But really. Ordering a criminal to spy for you?

02:34.400 --> 02:35.670
Of course.

02:36.330 --> 02:42.640
Why did you think I allow him so much freedom,
 albeit in a solitary cell?

02:43.500 --> 02:48.170
Now you have the name of your "mastermind."

02:48.170 --> 02:52.100
You can locate Senior Commissioner 
Habaki using our security cameras.

02:52.870 --> 02:56.050
How you use that knowledge is up to you.

02:56.530 --> 02:58.210
I see!

02:58.210 --> 03:01.990
So, you want me to do 
your dirty work for you!

03:01.990 --> 03:07.930
Aren't you after the man who had you 
shot at and whatever lies behind him?

03:08.870 --> 03:10.930
And one more thing.

03:10.930 --> 03:13.460
I'll pay for it, of course.

03:14.070 --> 03:15.540
What do you want?

03:16.490 --> 03:21.260
Inspector Tsubaki Iwanome's 
cell phone number.

03:25.530 --> 03:26.780
Solitaire?!

03:34.040 --> 03:35.130
Takumi-kun?

03:35.130 --> 03:36.650
<i>Oh! I got through!</i>

03:37.070 --> 03:40.500
I'll fill you in later, but be on your guard!

03:40.940 --> 03:42.990
We want to head back pronto,

03:43.200 --> 03:44.930
but we'll be a little delayed.

03:46.500 --> 03:47.470
What the...?!

03:48.660 --> 03:54.380
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

03:48.660 --> 03:54.380
...but my old country home!

03:55.920 --> 03:59.630
Saying your contact's 
name was beyond careless,

04:00.010 --> 04:01.390
Senior Commissioner Habaki!

04:02.330 --> 04:04.010
What are you talking about?

04:04.010 --> 04:07.190
You just said "Higuro", didn't you?

04:07.190 --> 04:10.470
Why were you talking with 
a Shibuya intermediary?

04:11.540 --> 04:12.560
You see—

04:12.560 --> 04:15.990
And who or what is "Sabaramond"?

04:17.600 --> 04:20.860
I really felt like I owed you.

04:20.860 --> 04:24.570
W-Wait! Sabaramond is—

04:27.790 --> 04:32.400
He said... "Sabaramond."

04:32.400 --> 04:34.000
I heard him say it.

04:34.410 --> 04:35.870
Who're these guys?!

04:36.090 --> 04:38.840
He said it. He said it.

04:39.260 --> 04:40.880
He said it.

04:40.880 --> 04:42.830
We heard him say it.

04:42.830 --> 04:45.470
He said it. He said it.

04:45.470 --> 04:47.260
Said, said, said, said, said, said, said.

04:48.010 --> 04:55.730
My old friends, are you still there?

04:56.890 --> 05:01.130
Sabaramond. He said it—said it.

05:01.130 --> 05:07.200
No mistake-ake-ake-ake-ake-ake-ake-ake.

05:10.940 --> 05:13.510
He's a bastard child.

06:47.420 --> 06:50.340
Bastard child-ild-ild-ild.

06:50.340 --> 06:54.680
B-B-Bastard child of S-Sabaramond-ond-nd-d.

06:54.680 --> 06:55.660
Boss.

06:57.870 --> 06:59.060
Hang on.

06:59.060 --> 07:00.260
Seriously?

07:00.770 --> 07:03.770
The luck of the draw's really 
been on your side, Boss.

07:03.770 --> 07:06.330
You've pulled Lemmings, Solitaire,

07:06.330 --> 07:08.000
and now the Fire-Breathing Bug.

07:08.410 --> 07:12.410
I'd say draws like these are 
what lose you the game.

07:12.670 --> 07:13.890
Damn it.

07:15.370 --> 07:24.710
In the rain and the blustery air,

07:24.710 --> 07:26.570
I think—

07:26.570 --> 07:30.300
"I think of my old country home," correct?

07:33.210 --> 07:38.680
Kindly disperse and withdraw, 
my feeble little bugs.

07:39.040 --> 07:41.900
My brother is a fool, but not a bastard.

07:42.220 --> 07:45.900
Burning him won't singe the world one bit.

07:46.700 --> 07:50.110
I won't help, and I won't hinder.

07:50.760 --> 07:55.330
I'll merely pity you and pray

07:55.570 --> 08:00.580
<b>Matriarch</b>

07:56.530 --> 08:00.580
for your long-sought revenge,

08:02.060 --> 08:04.610
so leave this place for my sake.

08:05.030 --> 08:08.800
Out of respect for Majiri Agakura.

08:08.800 --> 08:15.280
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

08:19.910 --> 08:21.640
Who were they?

08:21.640 --> 08:23.240
Do you know them, Ma-nee?

08:23.240 --> 08:26.230
Yes. We're something like friends.

08:27.530 --> 08:31.590
Don't go after those 
people in raincoats, now.

08:32.280 --> 08:36.600
You couldn't crush them all, 
no matter how hard you tried.

08:40.660 --> 08:42.000
What's wrong with them?

08:42.000 --> 08:44.500
They act like they can't see us.

08:44.710 --> 08:47.210
They must really hate Habaki.

08:47.520 --> 08:50.500
No. I can't afford to go down yet.

08:51.300 --> 08:52.090
Iwa-san.

08:52.400 --> 08:54.300
They're acting strangely.

08:55.610 --> 08:58.010
The secret to the 
Fire-Breathing Bug's tricks?

08:58.010 --> 09:04.810
Yes. If you won't turn yourself in, 
then pay me by explaining that.

09:06.890 --> 09:08.560
Just a hint, then.

09:08.560 --> 09:13.030
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

09:09.450 --> 09:13.400
The Fire-Breathing Bug 
is and is not one person.

09:13.840 --> 09:17.910
They're extremely close to 
being a psychic or a wizard,

09:17.910 --> 09:21.540
but what they are is a 
crystallization of technology

09:21.540 --> 09:24.250
that's left the realm of common sense.

09:26.960 --> 09:28.790
What the—?!

09:29.430 --> 09:30.990
Is this...? No way.

09:31.380 --> 09:32.280
Arase!

09:33.130 --> 09:35.340
Grab a fire extinguisher!

09:38.010 --> 09:39.430
Okay.

09:39.690 --> 09:40.260
Hey!

09:40.730 --> 09:43.460
Why was the Fire-Breathing 
Bug out to get you?!

09:43.460 --> 09:44.520
Damn!

09:44.890 --> 09:49.060
<i>Jeez. Solitaire's bad enough on his own.
 I don't need more magic tricks.</i>

09:49.540 --> 09:53.960
You guys are like a Gamma Knife.
 You know that?

09:53.960 --> 09:55.190
What's that?

09:55.190 --> 10:01.810
A machine that burns out tumors with 
hundreds of gamma rays from all sides.

10:01.810 --> 10:08.650
You follow thin trails of evidence 
to the point where they meet

10:08.650 --> 10:11.540
and incinerate a criminal 
in the fires of judgment.

10:12.880 --> 10:17.200
Of course, they get off 
scot-free when you misfire.

10:20.400 --> 10:23.850
<i>Our coroner's snide comments 
come in handy now and then.</i>

10:24.370 --> 10:27.810
<i>The Fire-Breathing Bugs are probably 
firing lasers or something, too.</i>

10:28.120 --> 10:29.770
<i>And where the beams converge—</i>

10:30.220 --> 10:34.110
<i>No, they're precise enough 
to write notes at a distance.</i>

10:34.110 --> 10:35.220
<i>No one could pull that off.</i>

10:36.860 --> 10:40.360
<i>Look at it another way. 
Forget what's "impossible".</i>

10:40.970 --> 10:43.830
<i>Everyone we've faced so far</i>

10:44.280 --> 10:46.600
<i>has redefined what's possible!</i>

10:49.130 --> 10:50.100
<i>Jeez.</i>

10:51.060 --> 10:55.210
<i>The way things are going, we'll run 
into a real monster one of these days!</i>

10:57.980 --> 11:00.000
For starters, let's get out of here.

11:00.330 --> 11:04.590
That asshole Higuro might 
call in reinforcements.

11:04.590 --> 11:06.650
What should we do with this guy?

11:07.370 --> 11:11.020
<i>The singing people are... gone?</i>

11:11.380 --> 11:12.760
<i>What could have—</i>

11:14.170 --> 11:15.390
Someone's coming.

11:17.120 --> 11:18.680
Maybe an enemy.

11:23.420 --> 11:24.570
Wow.

11:24.950 --> 11:26.170
He noticed us.

11:26.540 --> 11:29.170
And we were trying to be stealthy.

11:29.170 --> 11:31.000
Mm-hmm. Of course,

11:31.470 --> 11:33.960
he hasn't picked up on Ma-nee.

11:36.000 --> 11:37.670
It's been far too long,

11:38.130 --> 11:40.130
my lovely little

11:40.350 --> 11:42.840
boy assassin.

11:50.420 --> 11:54.580
I see your new prosthetic arms are well made.

11:56.900 --> 12:01.360
But didn't I tell you, dear little boy?

12:01.980 --> 12:04.200
Just become my little brother,

12:04.980 --> 12:07.910
and you can have your limbs 
back whenever you like.

12:09.930 --> 12:11.000
So...

12:12.400 --> 12:14.350
You really are back in Japan.

12:19.260 --> 12:21.520
<i>The job was supposed to be easy.</i>

12:22.460 --> 12:27.400
<i>Just a small-time target, 
perfect for my first assignment.</i>

12:28.560 --> 12:31.130
<i>But that small fry was also</i>

12:34.110 --> 12:37.050
<i>on someone else's hit list.</i>

12:38.320 --> 12:41.110
<i>"Kill anyone in the building."</i>

12:41.110 --> 12:43.610
<i>Those were my orders.</i>

12:44.490 --> 12:45.850
<i>I didn't hesitate.</i>

12:46.410 --> 12:48.680
<i>My blade lopped off the woman's head.</i>

12:49.370 --> 12:51.370
<i>Or I meant for it to.</i>

12:51.770 --> 12:55.910
I like how you go for the kill.
 And you're cute.

12:56.240 --> 13:00.380
You must be the Leis' latest killing machine.

13:01.400 --> 13:03.410
That settles it. I've decided.

13:03.410 --> 13:06.340
How would you like to become 
an Agakura by adoption?

13:06.730 --> 13:09.390
<i>I had no idea what she was talking about.</i>

13:09.910 --> 13:14.350
<i>But it was what came next 
that really baffled me.</i>

13:14.640 --> 13:17.930
The Heilei are awful, you know?

13:18.490 --> 13:21.190
You must have experienced that firsthand.

13:24.490 --> 13:27.920
<i>The next thing I knew, my arms and legs were gone.</i>

13:28.590 --> 13:32.410
<i>Strange as it sounds, 
I don't think I bled that much.</i>

13:32.690 --> 13:36.970
Don't worry. I fixed you up so you won't die.

13:37.420 --> 13:41.130
Still, I wonder what the 
Heilei will do with you.

13:41.690 --> 13:44.590
If you want help, call me.

13:45.560 --> 13:47.420
I'll come running,

13:48.250 --> 13:51.260
and I'll give your limbs back when I do.

13:51.260 --> 13:55.710
I'll give you lots of love 
as a new member of my family.

13:57.370 --> 14:00.030
Nee-san sure is fickle.

14:00.030 --> 14:03.550
Mm-hmm. But cutting off limbs is new.

14:03.550 --> 14:05.690
Ma-nee must really like him.

14:06.120 --> 14:09.620
Till we meet again,
 my lovely little assassin.

14:10.490 --> 14:12.160
My name is...

14:13.160 --> 14:15.020
Majiri Agakura!

14:15.020 --> 14:17.910
So, what will it be?

14:19.960 --> 14:23.540
You just called my name, didn't you?

14:24.050 --> 14:26.920
Do you want my help?

14:27.700 --> 14:28.900
Your help?

14:28.900 --> 14:31.240
If you join my family,

14:31.240 --> 14:36.260
I'll slaughter all those 
bothersome Heilei for you.

14:37.250 --> 14:40.730
You're right. I hate the Heilei Clan.

14:42.370 --> 14:43.190
But

14:43.700 --> 14:50.160
the blood—or the techniques—
I inherited don't bother me so much.

14:51.940 --> 14:54.920
More importantly, the place I belong

14:55.290 --> 14:57.370
isn't with the Heilei <i>or<i>

14:57.720 --> 14:59.330
This blood of mine</i></i>

15:01.370 --> 15:03.690
is lightning that protects the Shinoyamas!

15:06.430 --> 15:08.130
I miscalculated.

15:08.620 --> 15:13.350
I never dreamed the Shinoyamas would 
rescue you before I got the chance.

15:18.880 --> 15:20.970
Seriously, Majiri-neesan?

15:20.970 --> 15:23.940
You carried a torch for nearly a decade, 
and he turned you down?

15:24.320 --> 15:26.910
Oh, Momo-kun. You're alive.

15:27.240 --> 15:29.900
I'm so glad.

15:30.890 --> 15:34.920
But laughing at your big sister's 
broken heart isn't very nice.

15:35.520 --> 15:37.240
I'll scold you later.

15:37.620 --> 15:41.120
Right now, a punishment 
from you would kill me.

15:41.400 --> 15:44.410
He hurt you that badly?

15:45.080 --> 15:49.200
You've grown, my lovely little assassin.

15:49.200 --> 15:51.170
No, Neesan.

15:51.170 --> 15:53.150
I lost

15:53.150 --> 15:55.220
to the girl above you.

16:06.900 --> 16:09.510
Watch out, Nee-san.

16:09.510 --> 16:14.110
She must've learned from Solitaire. 
She has tricks up her sleeve.

16:17.420 --> 16:21.910
Momoya is small-time. 
The seventh-weakest Agakura.

16:21.910 --> 16:24.170
Doesn't that put him right in the middle?

16:28.330 --> 16:31.510
Thanks! That was nice of you!

16:31.900 --> 16:34.330
What's your name?

16:34.330 --> 16:37.040
Oh, I'm Misaki. Misaki Sakimiya!

16:37.040 --> 16:38.180
Nice meeting you!

16:38.910 --> 16:42.430
"Misaki Agakura." It has a nice ring to it.

16:42.760 --> 16:43.520
Huh?

16:44.050 --> 16:48.480
Would you consider bearing the Agakura name?

16:48.480 --> 16:52.420
<b>Misaki A. (Agakura) Sakimiya</b>

16:48.900 --> 16:50.980
As a middle name, sure.

16:50.980 --> 16:55.030
No, you should make "Sakimiya" 
your middle name.

16:52.460 --> 16:55.030
<b>Misaki S. (Sakimiya) Agakura</b>

16:55.510 --> 16:58.290
Could this conversation get any stupider?

17:00.060 --> 17:03.080
My sister really is fickle.

17:08.590 --> 17:10.340
I have no choice.

17:10.340 --> 17:14.440
My darling little brother 
will die without help.

17:15.410 --> 17:16.090
Kana.

17:16.090 --> 17:16.970
Mm-hmm.

17:18.550 --> 17:19.510
Dahlia.

17:29.520 --> 17:32.170
Dahlia, you take his weapon.

17:33.840 --> 17:36.050
Today was a draw.

17:36.660 --> 17:39.780
Let's leave it at that and split up.

17:40.280 --> 17:43.090
I'm so sorry for breaking you prosthetic arm.

17:43.090 --> 17:47.710
If you come visit, I'll give you 
the original to make up for it.

17:48.720 --> 17:52.170
Till we meet again, Misaki-chan.

17:58.480 --> 18:01.280
H-Hey. Should we have just let them go?

18:01.280 --> 18:06.310
I couldn't stop them.
 She took out one of my legs, too.

18:06.310 --> 18:09.570
Hmm... I don't think I was up to it, either.

18:10.310 --> 18:13.900
You know how Polka-kun 
stabbed me that one time?

18:13.900 --> 18:16.150
Huh? Oh, yeah.

18:16.480 --> 18:21.920
That lady's probably tougher 
than Polka-kun was then.

18:26.660 --> 18:30.670
I can't use my position anymore.

18:30.950 --> 18:33.390
Stand up, Senior Commissioner.

18:33.840 --> 18:35.050
Damn you!

18:35.750 --> 18:40.680
The Bug knows what I look like now!

18:42.930 --> 18:44.180
Powder?

18:44.830 --> 18:46.810
Hey! Did you just swallow that?!

18:47.230 --> 18:51.810
So I suppose it won't 
matter... if I cut loose.

18:52.770 --> 18:53.820
Huh?

18:55.160 --> 18:56.020
Iwa-san!

18:57.040 --> 18:58.030
Are you okay?

18:58.030 --> 18:59.960
Sorry. I owe you one.

19:00.990 --> 19:03.710
How did he get so strong?

19:07.520 --> 19:11.650
I can't afford... to die here.

19:12.660 --> 19:14.500
Some kind of drug, maybe?

19:14.820 --> 19:17.170
You've shown your true colors.

19:17.630 --> 19:21.800
Looks like we've got you 
red-handed now, huh?!

19:22.330 --> 19:24.650
There's nothing red about me.

19:24.650 --> 19:31.440
This world has yet... to be colored.

19:31.440 --> 19:37.380
Yes. Soon, the great one shall bore a hole!

19:37.750 --> 19:39.160
What's he talking about?

19:39.160 --> 19:40.650
He must be high.

19:41.100 --> 19:42.220
Now,

19:47.230 --> 19:49.580
who should we deal with first?

19:54.880 --> 19:57.550
I wonder if they'll be okay.

19:58.300 --> 20:00.360
It looks like lightning.

20:00.360 --> 20:01.510
Lightning...

20:03.670 --> 20:07.720
Oh. I thought elementals 
were sparse in this world,

20:08.240 --> 20:13.850
but the density of lightning elementals 
is about the same as in mine.

20:14.120 --> 20:16.100
Lightning elementals?

20:16.100 --> 20:19.340
Can you contract with them to cast spells?

20:19.340 --> 20:21.890
I'm not an elementalist.

20:22.890 --> 20:29.830
It's suicidal for a non-specialist to 
draw on lightning elementals directly.

20:30.690 --> 20:34.790
A handful of geniuses have 
pulled it off, though.

20:43.030 --> 20:46.230
Oh, I've grown fond of this.

20:46.230 --> 20:50.090
This land's elementals 
are quite the delicacy.

20:50.090 --> 20:53.690
Huh? I've got no clue what 
you're talking about, Boss!

20:53.690 --> 20:56.790
That thunder left my ears ringing!

20:56.790 --> 20:58.100
Ever think of that?!

20:58.100 --> 21:00.300
Oh, sorry about that.

21:02.390 --> 21:04.570
But I'm just so excited!

21:04.970 --> 21:09.030
That annoying Bug may be in this city, too,

21:09.030 --> 21:12.120
but everyone's done so much for us!

21:13.000 --> 21:15.580
And then there are the 
hands on that building!

21:16.290 --> 21:20.080
I never expected them to appear 
on this far-away island!

21:20.910 --> 21:23.440
Did they wrench open the 
hole from the other side?

21:23.770 --> 21:27.210
Or is this a whim of Ordom, 
the Destructive Wyvern?

21:28.130 --> 21:32.200
Umm... Are you sure about 
that symbol on your back?

21:32.200 --> 21:34.640
Why hide it anymore?

21:34.850 --> 21:38.040
A local stage magician already 
let that cat out of the bag.

21:39.320 --> 21:42.480
Oh, I can hardly wait!

21:43.210 --> 21:47.070
I've just <i>got</i> to track them down 
and roll out the red carpet...

21:54.280 --> 21:58.710
...to welcome our very first 
visitor from my homeland.
